+# ADR-0015: Read advisor master data from the ERP through the port
+
+- **Status:** Proposed
+- **Date:** 2026-11-04
+- **Deciders:** <to be set by the reviewers>
+- **Sources:** T3-D-005, T3-D-009, T3-AC-001, T2-D-009, TD-15, DP1 section 3.1
+
+## Context
+
+Head office needs the advisor master data. The ERP runs customer and advisor master data (DP1 section 3.1). Every module reaches the ERP only through the integration module and its port (T3-D-005, T3-AC-001). The port today has one operation, `readCustomer`. The `identity` module owns the person record with roles (T3-D-009), so it is the module that answers "who is this advisor". Every ERP read records its source, source version and read time (T2-D-009).
+
+## Options
+
+1. **Add `readAdvisor` to the port and read on each call.** A new payload contract `AdvisorMasterData` (advisor number `B` + 5 digits, given name, family name, e-mail, active flag, source version) and `ErpPort.readAdvisor`. `integration` exposes `readAdvisor` as an `ErpRead<AdvisorMasterData>`. `identity` receives `Integration` as a dependency and exposes `getAdvisor`. Good: smallest change, follows the ERP convention, no new table. Bad: every call reaches the ERP; an ERP outage fails the read.
+2. **Keep a read copy of advisors in `integration` (`erp_copy`) and refresh it.** Good: reads work while the ERP is down. Bad: needs a table, a refresh job and a sync run (TD-15), which this change does not need yet.
+
+## Decision
+
+We choose option 1. It adds one operation to the port contract and one dependency from `identity` to the `integration` public API, as the ERP convention prescribes. A read copy (option 2) can replace the direct read later without changing `identity.getAdvisor`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- `ErpPort` gains `readAdvisor`. Every adapter (`erp-fake` now, `erp-nav` and `erp-bc` later) must implement it. The NAV contract for advisor data must be agreed with Provital's NAV developer.
+- `createIdentity` requires an `integration` dependency. The worker injects it.
+- `getAdvisor` throws `ErpUnavailableError` when the ERP is down; the caller decides the fallback.
+- `identity` does not store advisor master data, so no table and no new personal data columns.
+- `pnpm arch` keeps enforcing that only `integration` imports `@provital/erp-port`, and that there is no cycle between `identity` and `integration`.
